@startuml
title T12-WF01 — AI CRM Lead Qualification Agent (Sequence)
autonumber
participant "RabbitMQ" as MQ
participant "n8n WF01\nQualification" as N8N
participant "NestJS Backend" as API
database "PostgreSQL" as DB
participant "Gemini API" as AI
participant "NestJS Review Module" as REVIEW
participant "NestJS Notification Service" as NOTIFY

MQ -> N8N: lead.qualification.requested(eventId, leadId)
activate N8N
N8N -> N8N: Validate event and idempotency key
alt Invalid event or already processed
N8N --> MQ: Reject/acknowledge according to consumer policy
N8N -> N8N: End as ignored/duplicate
else Valid new event
N8N -> API: GET lead details
API -> DB: Read lead
DB --> API: Lead profile
API --> N8N: Lead data
N8N -> API: GET interaction context
API -> DB: Read recent interactions
DB --> API: Interaction signals
API --> N8N: Context
N8N -> N8N: Normalize qualification input
N8N -> AI: Request structured qualification
AI --> N8N: intent, rationale, confidence
N8N -> N8N: Parse and validate output
N8N -> API: POST qualification callback (authenticated canonical API)
API -> API: Re-apply authoritative policy
API -> DB: Persist qualification result idempotently
alt confidence <= 0.80 or other review-required condition
API -> REVIEW: Create/ensure ReviewTask idempotently
REVIEW -> DB: Persist ReviewTask if missing
DB --> REVIEW: ReviewTask ID/status
REVIEW --> API: Canonical task reference
API --> N8N: Review required + task reference
N8N -> API: Request idempotent reviewer notification
API -> NOTIFY: Notify assigned reviewer
NOTIFY --> API: Notification result
else confidence > 0.80 and no mandatory review condition
API --> N8N: Qualification result accepted
end
N8N -> N8N: Build final execution result with correlation IDs
end
deactivate N8N
note over N8N,API
All API operations shown in this sequence are canonical requirements. NestJS controllers, DTOs, guards, persistence and tests must implement these contracts.
end note
@enduml
